        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: вылет",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "вылет (výlet) — \"a departure (of a flight)\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Вылет задержали на час. Výlet zaderzháli na chas. The departure was delayed by an hour."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Masculine; the stress is on вы- (vý-). Время вылета — departure time."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "вылет (výlet) is built from вы- 'out' and лёт 'flight', the root of летать 'to fly'. EtymDB lists взлёт from the same root, Proto-Slavic vŭzletŭ."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
